ui-options-duty-performance-label = Performance
ui-options-duty-low-end-mode = Low-end device mode
ui-options-duty-low-end-mode-tooltip =
    Lowers the heaviest settings at once so the game stays playable on weak PCs:
    minimum lighting and shadow quality, low-resolution rendering, simplified space background,
    no ambient occlusion, fewer particles, less audio work and a 60 FPS cap without VSync.
    It does not hide gameplay information - light, night vision and effects stay, just simpler.
    Turning it off restores your previous settings (except the ones you changed by hand while it was on).
    Positional audio (HRTF) switches after a game restart.
ui-options-duty-low-end-mode-warning = Applying takes a couple of seconds - the game may freeze briefly.
ui-options-duty-low-latency = Low network latency
ui-options-duty-low-latency-tooltip =
    Keep one world snapshot buffered instead of two: other characters and items lag behind the server
    by about 30 ms less, and the client has less prediction to redo.
    On an unstable connection (packet loss, ping spikes) the world may start to stutter - turn it off then.
